  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Includes a set of twelve binding models with leather and various papers and sewing supports, wooden boards, museum board.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">This reference set of binding models is based on Karen Hanmer's popular workshop "Biblio tech: reverse engineering historical and modern binding structures". The models remain uncovered and only partially completed so methods of board attachment, sewing, spine lining, and endsheet construction are visible. Each model measures approximately 13 x 9 x 1 cm.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The set is accompanied by a 45 page illustrated booklet outlining key structural features of each binding, and providing numerous references for further study.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="504" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Includes bibliographical references (p. 43-44).</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="505" ind1="0" ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Tacketed binding -- Ethiopian binding -- Medieval binding -- Leather fine binding -- Boarded binding -- Split board binding -- Simplified binding -- German case binding -- Nonadhesive paper case -- Crossed structure binding -- Sewn boards binding -- Scaleboard binding -- Instructional booklet.</subfield>
  </datafield>
